flowchart TB
  accTitle: Proposed B2 reference implementation architecture
  accDescr: Tool adapters emit execution events to an append-only recovery ledger. A failure classifier proposes a typed finding. The recovery governor checks policy and opens a child runner from a versioned parent snapshot in an isolated namespace. The child proposes a typed resolution. A validator checks evidence, dependencies and parent version before a compare-and-swap committer updates the parent. A separate compiler extracts guarded rule candidates from validated traces; the rule registry tests, promotes, invalidates or rolls them back. The language model proposes diagnoses and actions but does not own commits or rule promotion.
  T[Tool / action adapters] --> L[(Append-only recovery ledger)]
  T --> F[Failure classifier]
  F --> G[Recovery governor]
  P[(Parent state store)] --> G
  G --> S[Scoped child recovery runner]
  S --> V[Resolution validator]
  P --> V
  V --> C[Compare-and-swap parent committer]
  C --> P
  V --> RC[Compiler candidate extractor]
  L --> RC
  RC --> Q[Quarantine / shadow tests]
  Q --> R[Rule registry]
  R --> G
  M[Model: diagnosis and action proposals] -. suggestions .-> F
  M -. suggestions .-> S
  M -. no direct commit authority .-> C
